<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33054" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orsa</span></b> , ōrum, n.
		ordior. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Beginnings</i>, <i>commencements</i>,
				<i>an undertaking</i>, <i>attempt</i>: ut (di) orsis tanti operis successus prosperos
			darent, Liv. praef. <i>fin.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Orsa juvare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 1, 21</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic., <i>words</i>, <i>speech</i>
				(<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sic orsa vicissim Ore refert,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 435</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">10, 632</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 124</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 5,
				472</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Menandri, i. e. carmina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 4, 46</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
